# GS Director: verify on the M4

Whenever Paul asks to **fix, change, or finish** GS Director (`mobile/apps/gsDirector`), treat M4 device verification as part of the work — not an optional follow-up.

## Device

- Run on **Pauls iPad Pro (2) — iPad Pro 11-inch (M4)** (`00008132-0000193801B9001C`).
- Do not stop at the simulator. Do not use the 2018 A12X unless Paul named it or the task is thermal measurement.
- If both iPads are attached, pin `DIRECTOR_DEVICE_UDID=00008132-0000193801B9001C`. If the M4 is missing, stop and say so.

## How much testing

After the code change, run **as much of the suite that already exists** as the change can affect:

1. `./scripts/build-device.sh` so Maestro `clearState` has a device `.app`
2. `./scripts/test-unit.sh` when Swift logic changed
3. `node scripts/run-maestro.js --suite operator` on the M4 for product/UI/pipeline work

Quote the runner line that names the M4. Fix failures before handing back.

Simulator is for compile iteration only. Thermals on the A12X stay a separate series (Peltier rule).
